From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:55:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: tsl2583: Measure without an LSCI calibration

The CT819 probe fails when the unit's LSCI record is missing or not the
supported version, and the light sensor is then gone. That is the case
on the iPad Air: its device tree (J71, J72) has no SysCfg reference for
alsCalibration, only a zero-filled property. A record the driver cannot
use, as on any unit whose LSCI is not the expected version, should not
cost the sensor either.

Probe without a record instead, with a warning, and report the TSL258x
lux computation for such a unit: uncalibrated, at the part's default
integration time and gain. A record that is read keeps being used as
before; errors other than a missing or unusable record still fail the
probe.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c b/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c
index aa63284..809b54a 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/light/tsl2583.c
@@ -134,6 +134,8 @@ struct tsl2583_chip {
 	struct apple_als_calibration cal;
 	u16 integration_cycles;
 	bool needs_reinit;
+	/* The LSCI record was usable; without one lux is the TSL258x's. */
+	bool calibrated;
 };
 
 struct gainadj {
@@ -308,9 +310,14 @@ static int apple_als_load_calibration(struct tsl2583_chip *chip)
 	int i;
 
 	data = apple_als_read_calibration(dev, &len);
-	if (IS_ERR(data))
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(data),
+	if (IS_ERR(data)) {
+		ret = PTR_ERR(data);
+		/* No record at all is reported by the caller. */
+		if (ret == -ENOENT)
+			return ret;
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
 				     "failed to read LSCI calibration\n");
+	}
 
 	if (len < APPLE_ALS_CAL_HEADER_SIZE + info->cal_record_size ||
 	    len & 1 || data[1] != info->cal_version || data[2] != 1 ||
@@ -504,7 +511,7 @@ static int tsl2583_get_lux(struct iio_dev *indio_dev)
 
 	chip->als_cur_info.als_ch0 = ch0;
 	chip->als_cur_info.als_ch1 = ch1;
-	if (chip->info->apple) {
+	if (chip->info->apple && chip->calibrated) {
 		ret = apple_als_get_lux(chip, ch0, ch1);
 		if (ret >= 0)
 			chip->als_cur_info.lux = ret;
@@ -1393,10 +1400,21 @@ static int tsl2583_probe(struct i2c_client *clientp)
 
 	/* Load defaults before exposing the IIO device to userspace. */
 	tsl2583_defaults(chip);
+	/*
+	 * Not every unit has a usable record: the iPad Air's device tree
+	 * carries none. Without one the sensor still reports the TSL258x lux
+	 * computation, uncalibrated, at the part's default time and gain.
+	 */
 	if (chip->info->apple) {
 		ret = apple_als_load_calibration(chip);
-		if (ret)
+		if (ret == -ENOENT || ret == -EINVAL)
+			dev_warn(&clientp->dev,
+				 "%s LSCI calibration, lux is uncalibrated\n",
+				 ret == -ENOENT ? "no" : "unusable");
+		else if (ret)
 			return ret;
+		else
+			chip->calibrated = true;
 	}
 
 	pm_runtime_enable(&clientp->dev);
